ardopcf for Debian
==================

Installation
------------
After installing this package, ardopcf will be available at /usr/bin/ardopcf.

Documentation
-------------
Manual page: man ardopcf
Installed docs: /usr/share/doc/ardopcf/
  - BUILDING.md: Build instructions
  - Commandline_options.md: Complete command-line reference
  - Host_Interface_Commands.md: Host interface protocol
  - USAGE_linux.md: Linux usage guide
  - USAGE_windows.md: Windows usage guide
  - Troubleshooting.md: Common issues and solutions
  - And more...
Upstream docs: https://github.com/pflarue/ardop/tree/master/docs

Usage Notes
-----------
- Audio devices must be specified at invocation or configured via WebGUI
- Default WebGUI port is 8514 (host_port - 1)
- Log files are written to the start directory by default
- See /usr/share/doc/ardopcf/ for additional documentation

ALSA Configuration
------------------
ardopcf will look for ALSA devices named "ARDOP" if none are specified.
Create ~/.asoundrc to define custom ALSA devices.
Note: DMIX/DSNOOP plugins are not currently compatible with ardopcf.

Support
-------
Community: ardop.groups.io (free users subgroup)
Issues: https://github.com/pflarue/ardop/issues

